+// 512-thread CTA per SM (`docs/experiments/20261021_adjacent_walk/`).  These
+// walks read 6% of the row at V/k = 1024 yet are 8-11% of the cell in time,
+// i.e. latency, not traffic.  Coverage is unchanged: each group visits
+// `j, j+stride, j+2*stride, j+3*stride` and strides by `4*stride`, and the
+// scalar tail picks up where that leaves off.
